1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:07,500
Across 21 heat pump installs, 38 percent needed
a new electrical panel. Was it in your quote?

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:15,988
Those were cold-climate prototypes in a field test, not a
national survey, so that share is not the odds for your house.

3
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:27,663
Where electrical upgrades were needed, they alone ran $3,750 to
$8,970 in labour and materials, before the heat pump itself.

4
00:00:28,167 --> 00:00:39,004
For a 200-amp panel on its own, a retrofit cost report cites an
outside estimate of $1,954, plus wiring for each new circuit.

5
00:00:40,033 --> 00:00:44,858
What the whole install really costs is
the question the full inquiry takes on.
